    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d879">

                <pb facs="1173" n="1053" xml:id="pg1053"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/2195</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Denby</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-26"><hi rendition="#italic">January 26,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In compliance with the request in your
                    letter of January 24, 1922, LA 837.00/2184, orders will be immediately issued
                    directing the withdrawal of the Marine Corps garrison now at Camaguey, Cuba.</p>
                <p>This detachment will be withdrawn to the U.S. Naval Station, Guantanamo Bay,
                    Cuba, where it will complete its target practice and whence it will be returned
                    North on vessels of the Fleet early next spring.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin Denby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
